id: DRAFT-13491-lesspipe-2.27-toybox-file-mime-fallback
category: compat, platform, shell
build_system: shell|runtime
phase: runtime
match_keywords: file, --mime, Unknown option, mime, toybox file, libmagic, file -L -s -b, filetype detection, empty file type, gzip not detected, tar not detected, archive not recognized
error_signature: "file: Unknown option 'mime' (see \"file --help\") / file -L -s -b --mime returns empty output (toybox 0.8.12 has no libmagic MIME support)"
error_excerpt: "file: Unknown option 'mime' (see \"file --help\"); scripts relying on 'file --mime' get an empty type string, so every mime-dependent branch (gzip/bzip2/xz/zstd/tar/zip/jar/deb/ar/rar/7z) degrades to raw binary passthrough"
root_cause: "OHOS ships the toybox implementation of file(1) (toybox 0.8.12: only -bhLs options, no --mime, no libmagic MIME database). Upstream tools that branch on 'file --mime' output (lesspipe filetype(), other shell preprocessors) silently lose all file-type detection: the command substitution returns empty, the parsed ftype is empty, and compressed/archive files are echoed as raw binary."
rec_approach: "Add a fallback INSIDE the tool's filetype detection: when 'file --mime' returns empty, run the plain 'file -L -s -b' description and map it to the equivalent MIME type with a bash case statement (tar archive->application/x-tar, Zip archive->application/zip, gzip/bzip2/xz/zstd compressed->application/(x-)... ; ar archive->application/x-archive; 7-zip archive->application/x-7z-compressed; *text*->text/plain with charset=utf-8; directory->inode/directory; else application/octet-stream). For types toybox reports as plain 'data', probe magic bytes directly: 'Rar!' in the first 4 bytes -> application/x-rar. For Debian packages (ar archive containing a debian-binary member), read the first 32 bytes and match *debian-binary* -> application/vnd.debian.binary-package. Keep the GNU path untouched (the fallback only triggers when --mime fails), so the same script works on both GNU and OHOS systems."
solution: "See patches/0001-ohos-toybox-file-mime-fallback.patch in archives/l/lesspipe/2.27 — filetype() in lesspipe.sh gains a '[[ -z $ft ]]' guarded case-mapping block after the 'file --mime' probe. Verified by the upstream suite: before patch 41 passed / 20 FAILED, after patch 61 passed / 0 failed (73 auto-ignored for optional external tools)."
fallback: "If a GNU file/libmagic package is ever published to the registry, depending on it and putting it on PATH would restore the original detection without the mapping (larger footprint; the in-script mapping is dependency-free)."
prescan_pattern: "--mime"
verify_builds: "PR CI build (task #13491, lesspipe 2.27); local conan create ohos-aarch64: upstream suite 61/73/0, test_package smoke all passed"
severity: 2
last_updated: 2026-09-15
